1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,196
One prophet is named

2
00:00:01,196 --> 00:00:01,997
in the Quran

3
00:00:01,997 --> 00:00:03,158
more than any other.

4
00:00:03,158 --> 00:00:04,493
Not once or twice,

5
00:00:04,493 --> 00:00:05,399
but one hundred

6
00:00:05,399 --> 00:00:07,070
and thirty-six times,

7
00:00:07,070 --> 00:00:09,578
across thirty-four surahs.

8
00:00:09,578 --> 00:00:11,006
His name is Musa,

9
00:00:11,006 --> 00:00:12,527
peace be upon him.

10
00:00:12,527 --> 00:00:14,187
This is his story,

11
00:00:14,187 --> 00:00:15,163
told the way

12
00:00:15,163 --> 00:00:16,904
the Quran tells it.

13
00:00:16,904 --> 00:00:18,193
Surah Al-Qasas,

14
00:00:18,193 --> 00:00:19,284
the Stories,

15
00:00:19,284 --> 00:00:21,623
opens his story with a promise.

16
00:00:21,827 --> 00:00:23,487
Allah recites the news

17
00:00:23,487 --> 00:00:25,380
of Musa and Pharaoh in truth,

18
00:00:25,380 --> 00:00:27,173
for people who believe.

19
00:00:27,469 --> 00:00:29,234
It begins in Egypt,

20
00:00:29,234 --> 00:00:31,248
on the banks of the Nile.

21
00:00:31,544 --> 00:00:32,996
Pharaoh had made himself

22
00:00:32,996 --> 00:00:34,365
great in the land.

23
00:00:34,365 --> 00:00:36,560
He split its people into groups,

24
00:00:36,560 --> 00:00:37,570
and one group,

25
00:00:37,570 --> 00:00:38,916
the Children of Israel,

26
00:00:38,916 --> 00:00:39,834
he crushed.

27
00:00:39,834 --> 00:00:42,086
Their newborn sons were killed.

28
00:00:42,086 --> 00:00:44,094
Their daughters were left alive.

29
00:00:44,094 --> 00:00:45,569
But the Quran says

30
00:00:45,569 --> 00:00:47,902
Allah wanted something else.

31
00:00:47,902 --> 00:00:49,122
He wanted to favour

32
00:00:49,122 --> 00:00:50,828
the people who were oppressed,

33
00:00:50,828 --> 00:00:51,513
and to make

34
00:00:51,513 --> 00:00:53,951
them leaders and inheritors.

35
00:00:53,951 --> 00:00:55,437
Into this fear,

36
00:00:55,437 --> 00:00:57,492
a baby boy was born.

37
00:00:57,492 --> 00:00:58,491
His mother knew

38
00:00:58,491 --> 00:01:00,824
what happened to boys like him.

39
00:01:00,824 --> 00:01:02,496
Then Allah inspired

40
00:01:02,496 --> 00:01:04,133
her with an instruction

41
00:01:04,133 --> 00:01:06,095
that sounds impossible.

42
00:01:06,095 --> 00:01:07,105
Nurse him,

43
00:01:07,105 --> 00:01:09,021
and when you fear for him,

44
00:01:09,021 --> 00:01:10,612
cast him into the river.

45
00:01:10,612 --> 00:01:11,518
Do not fear

46
00:01:11,518 --> 00:01:13,015
and do not grieve.

47
00:01:13,015 --> 00:01:15,082
We will return him to you,

48
00:01:15,082 --> 00:01:15,999
and make him

49
00:01:15,999 --> 00:01:17,833
one of the messengers.

50
00:01:17,833 --> 00:01:19,331
So she placed her son

51
00:01:19,331 --> 00:01:20,399
in a chest

52
00:01:20,399 --> 00:01:22,512
and let the river take it.

53
00:01:22,512 --> 00:01:23,894
The water carried him

54
00:01:23,894 --> 00:01:24,718
away from her,

55
00:01:24,718 --> 00:01:25,949
downstream,

56
00:01:25,949 --> 00:01:26,970
toward the palace

57
00:01:26,970 --> 00:01:27,818
of the very man

58
00:01:27,818 --> 00:01:30,342
who was killing boys like him.

59
00:01:30,453 --> 00:01:31,719
The Quran describes

60
00:01:31,719 --> 00:01:33,948
her heart in one word:

61
00:01:33,948 --> 00:01:35,097
empty.

62
00:01:35,097 --> 00:01:37,721
She almost gave the secret away,

63
00:01:37,721 --> 00:01:40,281
but Allah held her heart firm.

64
00:01:40,391 --> 00:01:42,052
She said to his sister,

65
00:01:42,052 --> 00:01:43,346
follow him.

66
00:01:43,457 --> 00:01:44,374
The chest came

67
00:01:44,374 --> 00:01:45,871
to the bank by the palace,

68
00:01:45,871 --> 00:01:47,810
and Pharaoh's family lifted

69
00:01:47,810 --> 00:01:49,905
the baby out of the water.

70
00:01:49,947 --> 00:01:51,479
Pharaoh's wife said:

71
00:01:51,479 --> 00:01:52,803
a comfort of the eye,

72
00:01:52,803 --> 00:01:54,498
for me and for you.

73
00:01:54,498 --> 00:01:55,879
Do not kill him.

74
00:01:55,879 --> 00:01:57,528
Perhaps he will benefit us,

75
00:01:57,528 --> 00:01:58,561
or we will adopt

76
00:01:58,561 --> 00:01:59,850
him as a son.

77
00:01:59,850 --> 00:02:02,068
But the baby would not feed.

78
00:02:02,068 --> 00:02:03,136
Allah had kept

79
00:02:03,136 --> 00:02:05,486
every wet nurse from him.

80
00:02:05,690 --> 00:02:06,468
His sister,

81
00:02:06,468 --> 00:02:07,791
watching from a distance,

82
00:02:07,791 --> 00:02:09,126
stepped forward.

83
00:02:09,126 --> 00:02:09,800
Shall I show

84
00:02:09,800 --> 00:02:10,671
you a household

85
00:02:10,671 --> 00:02:12,324
that will care for him?

86
00:02:12,621 --> 00:02:14,154
And so Musa

87
00:02:14,154 --> 00:02:16,539
was returned to his own mother.

88
00:02:16,650 --> 00:02:17,556
The Quran says

89
00:02:17,556 --> 00:02:17,858
it was

90
00:02:17,858 --> 00:02:19,692
so that she would be content,

91
00:02:19,692 --> 00:02:20,899
and not grieve,

92
00:02:20,899 --> 00:02:21,538
and know

93
00:02:21,538 --> 00:02:22,293
that the promise

94
00:02:22,293 --> 00:02:24,306
of Allah is true.

95
00:02:24,858 --> 00:02:27,308
Musa grew up in Pharaoh's house.

96
00:02:27,308 --> 00:02:28,121
When he reached

97
00:02:28,121 --> 00:02:29,340
his full strength,

98
00:02:29,340 --> 00:02:30,350
Allah gave him

99
00:02:30,350 --> 00:02:32,236
judgement and knowledge.

100
00:02:32,440 --> 00:02:33,613
One day he entered

101
00:02:33,613 --> 00:02:35,261
the city at a quiet hour

102
00:02:35,261 --> 00:02:37,316
and found two men fighting,

103
00:02:37,316 --> 00:02:39,023
one from his own people,

104
00:02:39,023 --> 00:02:40,555
one from Pharaoh's.

105
00:02:40,555 --> 00:02:41,890
The man from his people

106
00:02:41,890 --> 00:02:43,458
called to him for help.

107
00:02:43,458 --> 00:02:45,106
Musa struck the other man,

108
00:02:45,106 --> 00:02:46,581
and the blow killed him.

109
00:02:46,581 --> 00:02:48,578
He had not meant to kill.

110
00:02:48,578 --> 00:02:49,959
Musa turned straight

111
00:02:49,959 --> 00:02:51,016
to his Lord.

112
00:02:51,016 --> 00:02:51,759
My Lord,

113
00:02:51,759 --> 00:02:53,245
I have wronged myself,

114
00:02:53,245 --> 00:02:54,290
so forgive me.

115
00:02:54,290 --> 00:02:56,078
And Allah forgave him.

116
00:02:56,078 --> 00:02:57,529
He is the Forgiving,

117
00:02:57,529 --> 00:02:59,137
the Merciful.

118
00:02:59,340 --> 00:03:00,733
The next day a man

119
00:03:00,733 --> 00:03:01,465
came running

120
00:03:01,465 --> 00:03:03,346
from the far end of the city.

121
00:03:03,346 --> 00:03:04,704
The leaders are plotting

122
00:03:04,704 --> 00:03:05,610
to kill you,

123
00:03:05,610 --> 00:03:06,307
he said.

124
00:03:06,307 --> 00:03:07,357
Leave.

125
00:03:07,468 --> 00:03:09,000
So Musa left Egypt

126
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:10,533
alone and afraid.

127
00:03:10,533 --> 00:03:11,717
He walked out across

128
00:03:11,717 --> 00:03:13,412
the desert toward Madyan,

129
00:03:13,412 --> 00:03:14,213
saying,

130
00:03:14,213 --> 00:03:15,931
perhaps my Lord will guide

131
00:03:15,931 --> 00:03:17,568
me to the right way.

132
00:03:17,568 --> 00:03:19,078
At the well of Madyan,

133
00:03:19,078 --> 00:03:20,215
shepherds crowded

134
00:03:20,215 --> 00:03:21,609
around the water.

135
00:03:21,609 --> 00:03:22,897
Off to one side,

136
00:03:22,897 --> 00:03:25,364
two women held their flock back.

137
00:03:25,660 --> 00:03:27,205
We cannot water until

138
00:03:27,205 --> 00:03:28,505
the shepherds leave,

139
00:03:28,505 --> 00:03:29,492
they said,

140
00:03:29,492 --> 00:03:30,490
and our father

141
00:03:30,490 --> 00:03:32,104
is an old man.

142
00:03:32,104 --> 00:03:33,126
Musa watered

143
00:03:33,126 --> 00:03:34,670
their flock for them.

144
00:03:34,670 --> 00:03:35,889
Then he went back

145
00:03:35,889 --> 00:03:36,690
into the shade

146
00:03:36,690 --> 00:03:38,594
and made a short prayer.

147
00:03:38,594 --> 00:03:39,477
My Lord,

148
00:03:39,477 --> 00:03:40,324
I am in need

149
00:03:40,324 --> 00:03:41,079
of whatever good

150
00:03:41,079 --> 00:03:42,814
You send down to me.

151
00:03:43,018 --> 00:03:43,935
A stranger,

152
00:03:43,935 --> 00:03:45,444
tired and alone,

153
00:03:45,444 --> 00:03:47,586
asking only for good.

154
00:03:47,998 --> 00:03:49,392
The answer came walking

155
00:03:49,392 --> 00:03:51,452
toward him with shyness.

156
00:03:51,748 --> 00:03:53,234
One of the women said,

157
00:03:53,234 --> 00:03:54,593
my father invites you,

158
00:03:54,593 --> 00:03:55,266
to reward

159
00:03:55,266 --> 00:03:57,135
you for watering our flock.

160
00:03:57,135 --> 00:03:58,088
Her father heard

161
00:03:58,088 --> 00:03:59,783
his story and told him:

162
00:03:59,783 --> 00:04:00,769
fear not.

163
00:04:00,769 --> 00:04:01,675
You have escaped

164
00:04:01,675 --> 00:04:03,399
the wrongdoing people.

165
00:04:03,509 --> 00:04:04,415
One of the daughters

166
00:04:04,415 --> 00:04:05,181
said, father,

167
00:04:05,181 --> 00:04:06,342
hire him.

168
00:04:06,342 --> 00:04:06,899
The best

169
00:04:06,899 --> 00:04:07,863
one to hire

170
00:04:07,863 --> 00:04:08,850
is the strong

171
00:04:08,850 --> 00:04:10,475
and the trustworthy.

172
00:04:10,475 --> 00:04:12,530
Her father offered Musa marriage

173
00:04:12,530 --> 00:04:13,877
to one of his daughters,

174
00:04:13,877 --> 00:04:15,734
for eight years of work,

175
00:04:15,734 --> 00:04:17,748
or ten if he chose.

176
00:04:17,789 --> 00:04:18,974
Musa stayed,

177
00:04:18,974 --> 00:04:20,999
and completed the term.

178
00:04:21,412 --> 00:04:22,491
Years later,

179
00:04:22,491 --> 00:04:23,583
Musa was travelling

180
00:04:23,583 --> 00:04:24,755
with his family through

181
00:04:24,755 --> 00:04:26,183
the dark desert.

182
00:04:26,183 --> 00:04:27,820
On the side of the mountain,

183
00:04:27,820 --> 00:04:29,318
he saw a fire.

184
00:04:29,318 --> 00:04:30,061
Stay here,

185
00:04:30,061 --> 00:04:31,036
he told them.

186
00:04:31,036 --> 00:04:32,139
Perhaps I can bring

187
00:04:32,139 --> 00:04:32,998
you a torch,

188
00:04:32,998 --> 00:04:34,368
or find some guidance

189
00:04:34,368 --> 00:04:35,448
at the fire.

190
00:04:35,448 --> 00:04:36,748
When he came to it,

191
00:04:36,748 --> 00:04:37,503
he was called

192
00:04:37,503 --> 00:04:38,141
from the right

193
00:04:38,141 --> 00:04:39,337
side of the valley,

194
00:04:39,337 --> 00:04:40,278
from a tree,

195
00:04:40,278 --> 00:04:41,845
in a blessed spot.

196
00:04:41,845 --> 00:04:43,133
O Musa.

197
00:04:43,133 --> 00:04:44,898
Indeed, I am your Lord,

198
00:04:44,898 --> 00:04:46,628
so remove your sandals.

199
00:04:46,628 --> 00:04:47,023
You are

200
00:04:47,023 --> 00:04:49,182
in the sacred valley of Tuwa.

201
00:04:49,182 --> 00:04:50,355
I have chosen you,

202
00:04:50,355 --> 00:04:52,433
so listen to what is revealed.

203
00:04:52,433 --> 00:04:53,826
I am Allah,

204
00:04:53,826 --> 00:04:55,858
there is no god but Me,

205
00:04:55,858 --> 00:04:57,205
so worship Me,

206
00:04:57,205 --> 00:04:58,470
and establish prayer

207
00:04:58,470 --> 00:05:00,310
for My remembrance.

208
00:05:00,513 --> 00:05:02,185
Then a question.

209
00:05:02,185 --> 00:05:02,650
What is

210
00:05:02,650 --> 00:05:04,263
that in your right hand,

211
00:05:04,263 --> 00:05:05,471
O Musa?

212
00:05:05,471 --> 00:05:06,713
It is my staff,

213
00:05:06,713 --> 00:05:07,468
he said.

214
00:05:07,468 --> 00:05:08,594
I lean on it,

215
00:05:08,594 --> 00:05:09,778
I bring down leaves

216
00:05:09,778 --> 00:05:10,811
for my sheep,

217
00:05:10,811 --> 00:05:11,717
and I have other

218
00:05:11,717 --> 00:05:13,029
uses for it.

219
00:05:13,029 --> 00:05:13,853
Throw it down,

220
00:05:13,853 --> 00:05:14,852
he was told.

221
00:05:14,852 --> 00:05:15,816
He threw it,

222
00:05:15,816 --> 00:05:17,197
and it became a snake,

223
00:05:17,197 --> 00:05:18,428
moving fast.

224
00:05:18,428 --> 00:05:20,564
Musa turned and ran.

225
00:05:20,564 --> 00:05:22,387
Come back and do not fear,

226
00:05:22,387 --> 00:05:23,328
he was told.

227
00:05:23,328 --> 00:05:24,152
Seize it.

228
00:05:24,152 --> 00:05:25,011
We will return

229
00:05:25,011 --> 00:05:26,723
it to what it was.

230
00:05:26,927 --> 00:05:28,900
Then a second sign.

231
00:05:28,900 --> 00:05:30,978
Put your hand into your garment,

232
00:05:30,978 --> 00:05:32,499
and it will come out white,

233
00:05:32,499 --> 00:05:34,334
without any illness.

234
00:05:34,334 --> 00:05:35,274
Two proofs,

235
00:05:35,274 --> 00:05:36,354
from your Lord,

236
00:05:36,354 --> 00:05:37,445
to Pharaoh.

237
00:05:37,445 --> 00:05:38,386
Go to Pharaoh,

238
00:05:38,386 --> 00:05:39,361
he was told.

239
00:05:39,361 --> 00:05:41,079
He has transgressed.

240
00:05:41,079 --> 00:05:43,273
Musa knew who Pharaoh was,

241
00:05:43,273 --> 00:05:44,191
and that they held

242
00:05:44,191 --> 00:05:46,129
a killing against him there.

243
00:05:46,129 --> 00:05:47,952
He did not refuse.

244
00:05:47,952 --> 00:05:49,601
He asked for help.

245
00:05:49,601 --> 00:05:50,414
My Lord,

246
00:05:50,414 --> 00:05:52,504
expand my chest for me,

247
00:05:52,504 --> 00:05:54,738
and ease my task for me.

248
00:05:54,942 --> 00:05:56,962
Untie the knot from my tongue,

249
00:05:56,962 --> 00:05:58,193
so that they understand

250
00:05:58,193 --> 00:05:59,249
my speech.

251
00:05:59,249 --> 00:05:59,795
And give me

252
00:05:59,795 --> 00:06:01,594
a helper from my family:

253
00:06:01,594 --> 00:06:03,736
Harun, my brother.

254
00:06:03,777 --> 00:06:05,240
Allah answered:

255
00:06:05,240 --> 00:06:05,867
you have been

256
00:06:05,867 --> 00:06:07,318
granted your request,

257
00:06:07,318 --> 00:06:08,554
O Musa.

258
00:06:08,757 --> 00:06:10,290
Then came an instruction

259
00:06:10,290 --> 00:06:11,532
worth remembering.

260
00:06:11,532 --> 00:06:12,519
Go, both of you,

261
00:06:12,519 --> 00:06:13,564
to Pharaoh,

262
00:06:13,564 --> 00:06:14,899
the man who said:

263
00:06:14,899 --> 00:06:17,488
I am your most exalted lord.

264
00:06:17,488 --> 00:06:19,473
Speak to him with gentle speech,

265
00:06:19,473 --> 00:06:20,390
so that perhaps

266
00:06:20,390 --> 00:06:21,737
he will remember,

267
00:06:21,737 --> 00:06:22,956
or fear.

268
00:06:22,956 --> 00:06:24,071
Gentle words,

269
00:06:24,071 --> 00:06:25,533
for the greatest tyrant

270
00:06:25,533 --> 00:06:26,822
of his time.

271
00:06:26,822 --> 00:06:28,146
In Pharaoh's court,

272
00:06:28,146 --> 00:06:29,214
Musa said:

273
00:06:29,214 --> 00:06:30,200
send the Children

274
00:06:30,200 --> 00:06:31,936
of Israel with us.

275
00:06:32,348 --> 00:06:33,521
Pharaoh answered

276
00:06:33,521 --> 00:06:34,624
with a question.

277
00:06:34,624 --> 00:06:36,168
Who is your Lord?

278
00:06:36,168 --> 00:06:37,433
Musa replied:

279
00:06:37,433 --> 00:06:38,118
our Lord

280
00:06:38,118 --> 00:06:39,187
is He who gave

281
00:06:39,187 --> 00:06:40,452
everything its form,

282
00:06:40,452 --> 00:06:42,269
and then guided it.

283
00:06:42,310 --> 00:06:43,599
Pharaoh gathered the most

284
00:06:43,599 --> 00:06:45,271
skilled magicians in Egypt

285
00:06:45,271 --> 00:06:46,339
on a festival day,

286
00:06:46,339 --> 00:06:47,918
before the crowds.

287
00:06:47,918 --> 00:06:49,102
They threw their ropes

288
00:06:49,102 --> 00:06:49,799
and staffs,

289
00:06:49,799 --> 00:06:51,227
and by their magic

290
00:06:51,227 --> 00:06:52,155
the ropes seemed

291
00:06:52,155 --> 00:06:54,308
to move like snakes.

292
00:06:54,512 --> 00:06:57,733
Musa felt fear inside himself.

293
00:06:57,775 --> 00:06:58,460
Fear not,

294
00:06:58,460 --> 00:06:59,470
Allah said.

295
00:06:59,470 --> 00:07:01,037
You are superior.

296
00:07:01,037 --> 00:07:01,711
Throw what

297
00:07:01,711 --> 00:07:03,475
is in your right hand.

298
00:07:03,475 --> 00:07:05,298
Musa threw his staff,

299
00:07:05,298 --> 00:07:06,993
and it swallowed everything

300
00:07:06,993 --> 00:07:08,224
they had made.

301
00:07:08,224 --> 00:07:09,838
The magicians knew magic

302
00:07:09,838 --> 00:07:11,707
better than anyone in Egypt,

303
00:07:11,707 --> 00:07:12,636
and they knew

304
00:07:12,636 --> 00:07:14,435
this was not magic.

305
00:07:14,435 --> 00:07:17,059
They fell down in prostration.

306
00:07:17,059 --> 00:07:17,744
We believe

307
00:07:17,744 --> 00:07:20,066
in the Lord of Harun and Musa.

308
00:07:20,066 --> 00:07:21,587
Pharaoh threatened to cut

309
00:07:21,587 --> 00:07:22,434
off their hands

310
00:07:22,434 --> 00:07:24,512
and feet and crucify them.

311
00:07:24,512 --> 00:07:25,592
They answered:

312
00:07:25,592 --> 00:07:27,682
decide whatever you will.

313
00:07:27,682 --> 00:07:29,156
You can only decide

314
00:07:29,156 --> 00:07:31,484
about this worldly life.

315
00:07:31,525 --> 00:07:34,021
Still Pharaoh refused.

316
00:07:34,021 --> 00:07:36,459
Allah sent signs upon Egypt:

317
00:07:36,459 --> 00:07:38,874
the flood, locusts, lice,

318
00:07:38,874 --> 00:07:40,453
frogs and blood.

319
00:07:40,453 --> 00:07:41,161
Each time,

320
00:07:41,161 --> 00:07:42,299
they begged Musa

321
00:07:42,299 --> 00:07:43,855
to pray for it to end,

322
00:07:43,855 --> 00:07:44,830
and promised to let

323
00:07:44,830 --> 00:07:46,188
his people go.

324
00:07:46,188 --> 00:07:47,570
Each time it ended,

325
00:07:47,570 --> 00:07:49,184
they broke their word.

326
00:07:49,184 --> 00:07:51,227
Then Allah told Musa:

327
00:07:51,227 --> 00:07:52,330
travel by night

328
00:07:52,330 --> 00:07:53,816
with My servants.

329
00:07:53,816 --> 00:07:55,813
You will be pursued.

330
00:07:55,813 --> 00:07:57,008
Pharaoh sent men

331
00:07:57,008 --> 00:07:59,586
to every city to gather an army,

332
00:07:59,586 --> 00:08:01,850
and they followed at sunrise.

333
00:08:01,850 --> 00:08:02,419
The sea

334
00:08:02,419 --> 00:08:03,580
was in front of them,

335
00:08:03,580 --> 00:08:05,588
and the army was behind.

336
00:08:05,588 --> 00:08:07,562
Musa's people cried out:

337
00:08:07,562 --> 00:08:09,304
we are going to be caught.

338
00:08:09,304 --> 00:08:10,976
Musa said: No.

339
00:08:10,976 --> 00:08:12,613
My Lord is with me.

340
00:08:12,613 --> 00:08:14,464
He will guide me.

341
00:08:14,575 --> 00:08:15,724
Those words,

342
00:08:15,724 --> 00:08:16,421
from a man

343
00:08:16,421 --> 00:08:18,151
with the sea at his back,

344
00:08:18,151 --> 00:08:19,300
are among the best

345
00:08:19,300 --> 00:08:20,972
known in the Quran.

346
00:08:20,972 --> 00:08:23,190
Allah inspired Musa:

347
00:08:23,190 --> 00:08:25,361
strike the sea with your staff.

348
00:08:25,361 --> 00:08:26,394
It split,

349
00:08:26,394 --> 00:08:27,776
and each side stood

350
00:08:27,776 --> 00:08:30,307
like a great towering mountain.

351
00:08:30,307 --> 00:08:32,002
A dry path opened

352
00:08:32,002 --> 00:08:33,012
through the middle,

353
00:08:33,012 --> 00:08:33,871
and Musa

354
00:08:33,871 --> 00:08:35,345
and all who were with him

355
00:08:35,345 --> 00:08:36,930
walked across.

356
00:08:37,040 --> 00:08:38,468
Pharaoh and his army

357
00:08:38,468 --> 00:08:39,699
followed them in.

358
00:08:39,699 --> 00:08:41,963
Then the sea closed over them.

359
00:08:41,963 --> 00:08:42,718
Musa and

360
00:08:42,718 --> 00:08:44,390
those with him were saved,

361
00:08:44,390 --> 00:08:45,841
all together.

362
00:08:45,841 --> 00:08:47,745
The others were drowned.

363
00:08:47,745 --> 00:08:49,765
As the water overtook him,

364
00:08:49,765 --> 00:08:51,751
Pharaoh finally said:

365
00:08:51,751 --> 00:08:52,389
I believe

366
00:08:52,389 --> 00:08:53,933
there is no god except

367
00:08:53,933 --> 00:08:55,083
the One the Children

368
00:08:55,083 --> 00:08:57,004
of Israel believe in.

369
00:08:57,045 --> 00:08:59,204
The answer came: now?

370
00:08:59,204 --> 00:09:01,480
When before you disobeyed?

371
00:09:01,480 --> 00:09:03,199
So today We will

372
00:09:03,199 --> 00:09:04,383
save your body,

373
00:09:04,383 --> 00:09:05,219
so that you may

374
00:09:05,219 --> 00:09:05,904
be a sign

375
00:09:05,904 --> 00:09:07,906
for those who come after you.

376
00:09:07,947 --> 00:09:08,957
Centuries later,

377
00:09:08,957 --> 00:09:10,002
the Prophet Muhammad,

378
00:09:10,002 --> 00:09:11,349
peace be upon him,

379
00:09:11,349 --> 00:09:12,568
came to Madinah

380
00:09:12,568 --> 00:09:14,495
and found the Jews fasting

381
00:09:14,495 --> 00:09:16,271
on the day of Ashura.

382
00:09:16,271 --> 00:09:17,038
They told him

383
00:09:17,038 --> 00:09:18,408
it was the day Allah

384
00:09:18,408 --> 00:09:19,580
saved the Children

385
00:09:19,580 --> 00:09:21,531
of Israel from their enemy,

386
00:09:21,531 --> 00:09:23,400
so Musa fasted it.

387
00:09:23,400 --> 00:09:24,213
He said:

388
00:09:24,213 --> 00:09:25,478
we have more claim

389
00:09:25,478 --> 00:09:27,069
over Musa than you.

390
00:09:27,069 --> 00:09:28,648
So he fasted it,

391
00:09:28,648 --> 00:09:30,006
and told the Muslims

392
00:09:30,006 --> 00:09:31,179
to fast it.

393
00:09:31,179 --> 00:09:32,084
It is recorded

394
00:09:32,084 --> 00:09:33,884
in Sahih al-Bukhari,

395
00:09:33,884 --> 00:09:36,142
number two thousand and four.

396
00:09:36,531 --> 00:09:38,371
Look back at the story.

397
00:09:38,644 --> 00:09:40,554
A mother who let go.

398
00:09:40,734 --> 00:09:42,615
A man who made a mistake,

399
00:09:42,615 --> 00:09:43,671
and turned straight

400
00:09:43,671 --> 00:09:45,140
back to Allah.

401
00:09:45,529 --> 00:09:47,038
A stranger who asked

402
00:09:47,038 --> 00:09:48,565
only for good.

403
00:09:48,838 --> 00:09:49,476
A prophet

404
00:09:49,476 --> 00:09:50,916
with a knot in his tongue,

405
00:09:50,916 --> 00:09:51,938
who asked for help

406
00:09:51,938 --> 00:09:53,650
instead of refusing.

407
00:09:53,854 --> 00:09:55,119
And gentle words,

408
00:09:55,119 --> 00:09:56,721
even for Pharaoh.

409
00:09:56,721 --> 00:09:57,430
When the sea

410
00:09:57,430 --> 00:09:59,705
was ahead and the army behind,

411
00:09:59,705 --> 00:10:01,017
he said only:

412
00:10:01,017 --> 00:10:02,689
my Lord is with me.

413
00:10:02,689 --> 00:10:04,825
That is the story of Musa.
